atlas surface

architecture saved-item
  canonical_name SavedItem
  family surface
  domain Surface / Personal Relation
  layer surface/public
  semantic_question What has this person chosen to keep, and what did its source say about it when they kept it?
  purpose Owns a signed-in person's private, reversible reference to a thing they kept -- a retained feed item or a property -- with the public description its source gave at that moment, so a kept thing outlives its source's latest feed slot for that person. Written only through the CMS binary from a one-type schema directory; read by the item page, the property page and /saved.
  maturity implemented
  consumes PageComposition
  consumes BonfyreAuth
  publishes SavedItem
  node_types SavedItem
  edge_types keeps
  invariant a saved item belongs to exactly one actor resolved from a valid BonfyreAuth session at request time; the page never trusts an actor named in a form or URL
  invariant saving is refused when the request's Origin is another site, and a session cookie is SameSite=Lax, so a cross-site form cannot keep something on a person's behalf
  invariant one actor keeps one thing once: the saved key is a digest of actor and item reference and the CMS enforces it unique
  invariant a snapshot holds only the public description the source gave (title, link, picture, publisher, maker, summary, observed time); it never holds a retained body
  invariant a kept item whose source has moved on is shown only to the person who kept it, marked as what the source published when they kept it; everyone else sees that it is not there any more
  invariant a page that knows its reader is never publicly cached (private, no-store; Vary Cookie)
  invariant unsave deletes the person's reference through the CMS binary; nothing else about the thing changes
  invariant a browser sign-in form returns the person to a validated same-site path (a next field, or the sign-in page's own next); any other destination falls back to the account page
  forbidden_inference a saved item -> a copy of the source's material, an endorsement, or a claim that the thing is true
  forbidden_inference a saved property -> a title search, an appraisal, an ownership interest or an opportunity opened in the work graph
  forbidden_inference a saved item -> membership, authority or any grant beyond the person's own reference
  forbidden_inference an item shown from a snapshot -> the source still publishing it
  known_gap Save is a native owner handler, not yet an ObjectGrammar contract offered through /_aperture; it should become one so the same aperture law governs it
  known_gap there is one collection (Saved); named boards and sharing a collection are not built
  known_gap a snapshot is private; a lawful path to promote a kept retained item into a canonical subject through an ObjectGrammar ATTACH birth is not built
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/saved_item.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/login.html
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_saved_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_parcel_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_saved_test.sh signs two people up through /signup and /login, proves an anonymous save redirects to sign in and back, a signed-in item page offers a real Save form and is privately cached, a cross-site save is refused and keeps nothing, saving twice keeps one row, the saved page lists and opens the item, another person cannot see it, the kept item survives its removal from the source feed for its keeper only, a browser sign-in form returns to next (and never to another site), and unsave removes it
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_parcel_test.sh saves a Tarrant property, lists it on /saved with its title-cased address and opens /s/parcel/<account>
  witness 2026-09-17 estate canary against copied CMS and auth stores signed a canary person up, saved a retained item and a property, listed both, refused a cross-site save, unsaved, returned a form sign-in to /saved with a session cookie, and walked 300 internal links with 0 dead anchors; production then registered saved_item through the CMS binary after a store backup (0 rows) and answered a failed form sign-in back to /login?next=/saved&failed=1
  source_lineage 2026-09-17 Pass 1 public-product convergence: real Save and continuity

interaction saved-item-keeps-public-subjects
  source page-composition
  destination saved-item
  relation keeps_reference
  preserves item page key or property account, the source's public description at the moment of keeping, the actor from a verified session
  drops retained source bodies, other people's keeps, source availability after the moment of keeping
  forbidden_inference a kept reference -> source truth, rights to the material or a canonical subject
  invalidates_on saved_item rows for that actor, the item's source material, BonfyreAuth session validity
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/page_saved_test.sh
